[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/897","id":4148344444,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSeuyxc73QrZ8","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/897","diff_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/897.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/897.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/issues/897","number":897,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat: applications page pipeline redesign with unified contacts, reminders, and status notes","user":{"login":"saeedkolivand","id":51081940,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDgxOTQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51081940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nFull Applications page upgrade — the layout locked in the design grill (pipeline strip + list), plus the data-model work it surfaced.\n\n**UI**\n- Pipeline strip: 6 glass stat cards (Saved · Applied · Screening · Interviewing · Offer · Closed) — click = filter; Closed aggregates rejected/ghosted/withdrawn with per-row stage tags when filtered; overdue follow-up badge on the strip.\n- Richer rows: date, board chip, doc count, next-action/overdue tag; sort control; flat list under any active filter (`activeStages !== null`), stage-sectioned when unfiltered.\n- Interaction log: `setStatus({note})` finally has UI — optional note on stage change (`StatusNoteModal`) + \"Add note\" writing a same-status event; timeline interleaves notes.\n- Detail panel: contact card, promoted reminder field, timeline with notes.\n- Skeletons share the strip's real class constants — 0.0px layout shift at all three text scales.\n\n**Data/backend**\n- Contact unification migration: `recipientName/Email` + `contactName/Email` merged into one canonical contact pair (backfill prefers `contact*`); ApplyByEmailTab and Overview read/write the same fields.\n- Reminders: due/overdue `nextActionAt` posts to the notification center with the existing `/applications?highlight=` deep link; checked on app start + periodic timer.\n\n**A11y/design-system hardening that fell out of review**\n- `use-focus-trap`: pre-open element captured in a layout effect; `autoFocus` removed from dialog content (it defeats return-focus — React applies it during commit, before any effect); pinned by tests including a real-trigger Escape→restore path.\n- Light-scheme contrast: canonical `utilities.css` light block remapped (`text-red-400` → red-700, `text-amber-400` → amber-800, `text-brand-soft` → canonical brand) — all audited readings now ≥4.5:1; probe asserts exactly one light rule per class so silent shadowing can't recur.\n- State styling on `.surface-card` descendants via `ring-*` (the unlayered utilities layer makes `bg-*`/`border-*` state dead); real `_one`/`_other` plurals in both locales.\n\n## Review trail\n\nAuthor → `frontend-reviewer` → `ui-ux-expert` (3 rounds, empirical: headless-Chromium measurements at 900×600/1440×900, dark+light, three text scales, pixel diffs) → final re-verify: **APPROVE — PR-ready**. Focus-restore, contrast, dedup-headers, skeleton-shift all measured fixed; advisory LOW (German label truncation at large scale) fixed via `title` attr in `b5a46562`.\n\n## Verification\n\n`pnpm format:check` 0 · `lint:strict` 0 · `typecheck` 13/13 · `pnpm test` 391 files / 4417 tests · `cargo fmt --check` 0 · clippy `--all-targets --all-features --locked -D warnings` 0 · `cargo test --locked` 2832 passed / 26 ignored · paint probes 13/13 + 17/17 — all re-run on the merged tree (zero-conflict merge with `origin/main` through #895, overlapping files verified semantically).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Migration bumps the dev DB; devs on old dev DBs may need to delete it (see docs note in the close-out PR).\n- Accepted follow-ups (tracked in the follow-ups ledger): narrow-width row density `@container` mitigation, company-avatar light contrast bump, ADR-0001 \"grouped list\" supersession note.\n- Branch is 1 generated-file commit behind main (`chore: update export benchmark data [skip ci]`) — zero overlap.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added an application pipeline overview with stage filtering, overdue follow-ups, and sorting options.\n  * Added background reminders for due and overdue follow-ups, with links directly to applications.\n  * Added optional notes after status changes and improved timeline note presentation.\n  * Added salary range formatting and improved application detail editing behavior.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved contact-field consistency during imports and updates.\n  * Added stronger validation for contact names and email addresses.\n  * Improved deep links, focus restoration, reduced-motion support, and error handling.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-07-28T04:50:21Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T05:41:12Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"cf57cbdfc15c9218a40073c89e334ecc0f8313df","assignees"